class:: LFCC
summary:: Linear frequency cepstral coefficients
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/MFCC2

description::
The filter points are equally spaced in Hz. LFCC is the linear-frequency control case for the conventional filterbank/log/DCT cepstral pipeline.

The pipeline is raw FFT magnitude/power, triangular bands in Hz, natural logarithm with a floor, then DCT-II. Coefficient c is sum(logBand[j] * cos(pi*(j+0.5)*c/numBands)). Orthonormal mode multiplies c=0 by sqrt(1/numBands) and all other coefficients by sqrt(2/numBands). Optional liftering multiplies coefficient c by 1 + lifter/2 * sin(pi*c/lifter). This shares the DCT formula and normalization with MFCC2.

Silence has the finite logFloor-derived c0 and approximately zero higher coefficients; omitting c0 removes that constant term. All parameters except chain are initialization settings. Memory is 8*numBands*(fftSize/2+1) bytes plus work arrays; cost is O(numBands*fftSize + numCoeffs*numBands) per FFT frame. It adds no lookahead beyond the FFT. Narrow unresolved bands return logFloor before the DCT.

Like vanilla link::Classes/MFCC::, this turns a spectral envelope into cepstral coefficients; the linear Hz spacing and explicit spectrum, normalization, and c0 options make the representation different.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain whose buffer matches fftSize.
argument:: numCoeffs
Literal integer 1..64; cannot exceed the available DCT coefficients.
argument:: numBands
Literal integer 4..128. Default 40.
argument:: minFreq
Lowest filterbank edge, in Hz.
argument:: maxFreq
Highest filterbank edge in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.
argument:: include0
Literal 1 includes c0; 0 starts at c1 and requires numCoeffs less than numBands.
argument:: normalize
Positive divides each triangular filter by its sum of sampled weights; 0 uses sums.
argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 magnitude or 1 power. Default 1.
argument:: logFloor
Positive lower floor before natural log, default 1e-10.
argument:: dctNorm
Positive selects the orthonormal DCT; 0 uses the unnormalized sum.
argument:: lifter
Positive sinusoidal lifter length; 0 disables liftering.
argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two 256..8192, matching the FFT buffer.
returns::
numCoeffs control outputs in increasing coefficient order.

examples::
LFCC calculates cepstral coefficients using linearly spaced triangular filter banks. In this example, it drives an overtone multiplier bank tracking chordal acoustics: linear cepstral shapes control resonance across an auxiliary bank of tuned comb filters, enhancing harmonic bloom on piano chords. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.bars:: displays the 13 linear cepstral coefficients in real time.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 13);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var lfcc = LFCC.kr(chain, numCoeffs: 13, numBands: 32, minFreq: 60, maxFreq: 8000, include0: 1, fftSize: 1024);
        var c1 = lfcc[1].lag(0.04);
        var c2 = lfcc[2].lag(0.04);

        // Linear spectral resonance comb filter
        var decayTime = c1.linlin(-20, 20, 0.2, 1.2).clip(0.1, 2.0);
        var combTuning = c2.linlin(-15, 15, 0.005, 0.02).clip(0.002, 0.03);
        var resonantBloom = CombC.ar(source, 0.05, combTuning, decayTime) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + resonantBloom;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, lfcc) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.bars("LFCC Coefficients", ~mir2Bus, 13, -30.0, 30.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

